<%= render "admin/reimbursements/shared/year_selector" %>
<%= render "admin/reimbursements/shared/cost_centre_selector" %>

<p class="mb-4 text-gray-600">
  <%# The one paragraph a successor reads first. It names the weekly loop in
      the order it is done, because the sidebar groups say what the screens
      are and nothing said what the JOB is. %>
  What the reimbursements portal is waiting on you for. The weekly loop is
  <strong>review</strong> the claims people have filed, <strong>build a batch</strong> of the
  approved ones, then <strong>send the EUSA draft</strong> it puts in your Outlook drafts. Once a
  month EUSA's actuals export arrives and you <strong>reconcile</strong> it against the ledger.
  <%# The front door is where a successor starts, so the glossary is named
      here before any of the screens that use its words. %>
  New to this? <%= link_to "What the words mean", admin_reimbursements_glossary_path,
                           class: "underline" %>.
</p>

<%= render CardComponent.new(title: "Claims") do %>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
    <%= render "stat",
               label: "To approve",
               count: @home.to_approve.size,
               amount: @home.to_approve_total,
               detail: "Yours to decide.",
               tone: :warning,
               link_text: "Review claims",
               path: admin_reimbursements_review_path(tab: "to_approve",
                                                      cost_centre: selected_cost_centre&.key) %>
    <%= render "stat",
               label: "Waiting on a budget owner",
               count: @home.awaiting_owner.size,
               amount: @home.awaiting_owner_total,
               detail: "Owners are reminded on this centre's run days; you can override.",
               link_text: "Awaiting owner",
               path: admin_reimbursements_review_path(tab: "awaiting_owner",
                                                      cost_centre: selected_cost_centre&.key) %>
    <%= render "stat",
               label: "Approved, ready to batch",
               count: @home.approved.size,
               amount: @home.approved_total,
               detail: "What the next BACS spreadsheet would pay.",
               link_text: "Build batch",
               path: new_admin_reimbursements_batch_path(cost_centre: selected_cost_centre&.key) %>
  </div>
<% end %>

<%= render CardComponent.new(title: "The last batch", html_class: "mt-4") do %>
  <% if @home.last_batch.nil? %>
    <p class="text-gray-600">
      No batch has been built yet. Approve some claims, then build a batch: that writes the BACS
      spreadsheet, puts a covering email in this cost centre's Outlook drafts, and marks the
      claims as sent to EUSA.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2">
      <%= link_to "Build batch",
                  new_admin_reimbursements_batch_path(cost_centre: selected_cost_centre&.key),
                  class: btn_classes(:secondary, :sm) %>
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <% batch = @home.last_batch %>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2">
      <span class="font-medium">BACS <%= reimbursements_date(batch.date_sent) %></span>
      <span class="text-sm">
        <%= pluralize(@home.last_batch_expenses.size, "claim") %>
      </span>
      <span class="text-sm font-medium tabular-nums">
        <%= reimbursements_money(@home.last_batch_total) %>
      </span>
      <% if batch.eusa_draft_created %>
        <%= render BadgeComponent.new(type: :success, pill: true).with_content("EUSA draft created") %>
      <% else %>
        <%= render BadgeComponent.new(type: :warning, pill: true).with_content("No EUSA draft: needs a look") %>
      <% end %>
      <%= link_to "Batch detail", admin_reimbursements_batch_path(batch.record_id),
                  class: btn_classes(:secondary, :sm) %>
      <%= link_to "All batches",
                  admin_reimbursements_batches_path(cost_centre: selected_cost_centre&.key),
                  class: btn_classes(:secondary, :sm) %>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
      <%# The portal records that it CREATED the draft; nothing records that
          anybody sent it. Saying so is the difference between a status and a
          guess, and sending it is the one manual step left in paying people. %>
      The portal creates the draft; a person still has to open Outlook and send it. Nothing here
      records whether that happened.
    </p>
  <% end %>
<% end %>

<div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2">
  <%= render CardComponent.new(title: "EUSA ledger") do %>
    <p class="mb-3 text-sm text-gray-600">
      Imported ledger rows that no budget's figures account for — not linked to a claim, not
      booked against an income line, and not one leg of an offsetting pair. Until they are
      linked, that money is missing from every budget total.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-3">
      <span class="text-2xl font-semibold tabular-nums <%= "text-warning" if @home.unattributed_count.positive? %>">
        <%= @home.unattributed_count %>
      </span>
      <span class="text-sm text-gray-700">
        <%# NET, and it can legitimately be negative (more unattributed income
            than spend) — which is why the count is printed beside it rather
            than the figure standing alone. %>
        unlinked, net <%= reimbursements_money(@home.unattributed_total) %>
      </span>
    </p>
    <% if @home.unattributed_preview.any? %>
      <ul class="mb-3 flex flex-col gap-1 text-sm">
        <% @home.unattributed_preview.each do |actual| %>
          <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2">
            <span class="text-gray-500"><%= reimbursements_date(actual.date) %></span>
            <span class="grow"><%= actual.narrative.presence || actual.ref.presence || "(no narrative)" %></span>
            <%# Debit and credit are printed apart, as the ledger prints them:
                netting one row to a bare negative would read as bad news for
                what is simply income nobody has booked to a line yet. %>
            <% if actual.debit&.positive? %>
              <span class="tabular-nums"><%= reimbursements_money(actual.debit) %></span>
            <% else %>
              <span class="tabular-nums"><%= reimbursements_money(actual.credit) %> in</span>
            <% end %>
          </li>
        <% end %>
        <%# The count above is the whole list and this is the first few of it,
            so the difference has to be on screen: a "7 unlinked" heading over
            five rows reads as a page that has lost two. %>
        <% hidden = @home.unattributed_count - @home.unattributed_preview.size %>
        <% if hidden.positive? %>
          <li class="text-gray-500">and <%= pluralize(hidden, "more row") %> on the Ledger</li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    <% end %>
    <p class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      <%= link_to "Ledger", admin_reimbursements_actuals_path(cost_centre: selected_cost_centre&.key),
                  class: btn_classes(:secondary, :sm) %>
      <%= link_to "Reconcile a new export", admin_reimbursements_reconciliation_path,
                  class: btn_classes(:secondary, :sm) %>
    </p>
  <% end %>

  <%= render CardComponent.new(title: "Budget health") do %>
    <p class="mb-3 text-sm text-gray-600">
      Lines with nothing left against their current plan — what has been approved, sent or paid
      is already past the figure the committee agreed, as revised.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-3">
      <span class="text-2xl font-semibold tabular-nums <%= "text-danger" if @home.over_budget_count.positive? %>">
        <%= @home.over_budget_count %>
      </span>
      <span class="text-sm text-gray-700">
        <%= "line".pluralize(@home.over_budget_count) %> over budget
      </span>
    </p>
    <% if @home.over_budget_preview.any? %>
      <ul class="mb-3 flex flex-col gap-1 text-sm">
        <% @home.over_budget_preview.each do |budget| %>
          <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2">
            <%= link_to budget.display_name,
                        edit_admin_reimbursements_budget_path(budget.record_id),
                        class: "grow underline" %>
            <span class="tabular-nums text-danger">
              <%# -remaining, because "£412.00 over" is how it is written
                  everywhere else here and a bare negative reads as bad news
                  twice. %>
              <%= reimbursements_money(-budget.remaining) %> over
            </span>
          </li>
        <% end %>
        <% hidden = @home.over_budget_count - @home.over_budget_preview.size %>
        <% if hidden.positive? %>
          <li class="text-gray-500">and <%= pluralize(hidden, "more line") %> over budget</li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    <% end %>
    <p class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      <%= link_to "Budget overview",
                  overview_admin_reimbursements_budgets_path(year: selected_financial_year&.key,
                                                             cost_centre: selected_cost_centre&.key),
                  class: btn_classes(:secondary, :sm) %>
      <%= link_to "Budgets",
                  admin_reimbursements_budgets_path(year: selected_financial_year&.key,
                                                    cost_centre: selected_cost_centre&.key),
                  class: btn_classes(:secondary, :sm) %>
    </p>
  <% end %>
</div>

<%= render CardComponent.new(title: "Reminder emails", html_class: "mt-4") do %>
  <p class="mb-3 text-sm text-gray-600">
    On each cost centre's run days the portal emails its finance address about claims stuck
    waiting for approval and about the queue ready to batch, and emails each budget owner who
    has a claim waiting on them. A blank date means it has never completed a run.
  </p>
  <ul class="flex flex-col gap-1 text-sm">
    <% @home.reminder_cost_centres.each do |centre| %>
      <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2">
        <span class="grow"><%= centre.name %></span>
        <span class="text-gray-600">
          last run
          <%= centre.last_nightly_run_on ? reimbursements_date(centre.last_nightly_run_on) : "never" %>
        </span>
      </li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
  <p class="mt-3">
    <%= link_to "Email & integrations", admin_reimbursements_status_path,
                class: btn_classes(:secondary, :sm) %>
  </p>
<% end %>

<p class="mt-4 text-sm text-gray-500">
  Claim totals here are the gross amounts EUSA pays. Budget figures exclude VAT, so they can be
  lower than the amounts people claimed.
</p>
